### Page 1 of 3

```text
CONTRACT NO. ________

THIS AGREEMENT, made and entered into this ________ day of ____________________,
2013, by and between the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a municipal corporation organized under the laws
of the State of Wyoming, acting by and through its political subdivision, the Cheyenne Police
Department, hereinafter referred to as the “Department,” whose address is 2101 O’Neil Avenue,
Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001, and the Laramie County School District No. 1, hereinafter referred to as the
“District,” whose address is 2810 House Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.

WITNESSETH:

WHEREAS, the District has identified the need for police services at various schools and school-
related events under its control and supervision; and

WHEREAS, the Department is a municipal police agency engaged in providing police services to
the City of Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS, the District desires to obtain the police services of the Department, and the
Department desires to provide said services.

NOW, THEREFORE, IN CONSIDERATION of the mutual promises and covenants hereinafter
contained, the parties agree as follows:

1.
This Agreement shall be in effect from August 27, 2013, through June 6, 2014.  The
Department shall have no obligation under this Agreement to provide police services to the District at any
school location during any time that such school location is closed by official action of the District.
Except as provided in this Agreement, the Department shall have no obligation to provide police services
to the District, as described in this agreement, beyond the hours provided for in this agreement.

2.
The Department shall appoint a representative who shall be responsible for managing and
coordinating the Department’s performance under this Agreement, and shall identify this representative to
the District by name and telephone number.

3.
The Department agrees to provide routine police services to the District under the terms
and conditions herein contained.  The duties assumed by the Department under this Agreement are duties
owed generally to the public, and by entering this Agreement, the Department does not assume any other
duty to the District, nor does the Department assume any duty to any particular individual.  The parties
agree that this Agreement does not create an agency relationship between the Department and the District,
and no representations of any kind, type or nature made by one party shall be binding upon or create a
duty in the other party.

4.
In return for police services to be provided by the Department pursuant to this
Agreement, the District agrees to pay to the City Treasurer the sum of Four Hundred Thirty-Five
Thousand, One Hundred Eighty-Five Dollars and Ten Cents ($435,185.10), which is equal to 75% of base
salary and benefits for seven officers and one sergeant.    Said sum shall be paid within thirty (30) days
after the execution of this Agreement.   In addition, the District shall reimburse the Department for
overtime costs incurred by the Department in the performance of services described in Paragraph 11.b., of
this Agreement at the rate of Forty Dollars ($40.00) per hour.
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
5.
All costs incurred by the Department in the performance of duties under this Agreement
shall be paid by the Department, including salaries and wages, and the District shall reimburse the
Department for all such costs up to the maximum of Four Hundred Thirty-Five Thousand, One Hundred
Eighty-Five Dollars and Ten Cents ($435,185.10) set forth in Paragraph 4 of this Agreement, except that
overtime costs for services provided under Paragraph 11.b., of this Agreement shall be in addition to the
maximum set forth in Paragraph 4.

6.
Police officers assigned to provide services under this Agreement shall, at all times, be
employees of the City of Cheyenne Police Department.  The Department shall comply with all federal,
state, and local laws and ordinances regarding the employment relationship between the City of Cheyenne
and police officers assigned to provide services under this Agreement.

7.
The District and Department are aware that each party to this Agreement is subject to the
supervision of separately elected political entities.  Each party to this Agreement obtains funding which is
subject to annual budget approval.   Each party hereto shall notify the other immediately if a party’s
future fiscal year funding for this Agreement is curtailed or eliminated.

8.
Each party hereto shall be responsible for its own negligence and the negligence of its
agents, employees, representatives and other personnel.  The Department is a participant in the Wyoming
Association of Risk Management (WARM) and is insured by WARM to the limits described in the
Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, Wyo. Stat. §§ 1-39-101 through 1-39-120 (1988), as amended.  The
City and the District do not waive any applicable defenses and expressly reserve the right to invoke
governmental immunity pursuant to the Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, Wyo. Stat. 1-39-101, et
seq. for any claims arising out of performance of this agreement.

9.
The Department personnel provided by the Department pursuant to this Agreement shall
be directly supervised by the Department’s Patrol Commander.  Department personnel provided pursuant
to this Agreement will coordinate their activities with the principal of each of the District’s schools
identified herein.   Department personnel provided pursuant to this Agreement will be subject to other
assignments in times of emergencies, as determined by the Department.  In selecting personnel to provide
services pursuant to this Agreement, the Department shall consider each officer’s interest in the
assignment, ability to deal with the District’s students, and any special training which may have been
received.

10.
Department personnel providing services pursuant to this Agreement shall conduct
themselves as police officers and shall at all times follow the policies and procedures of the Department.

11.
The Department shall provide routine police services to the District at the following
locations and at the following times:

a.
Seven officers and one Sergeant stationed variously at High Schools, Junior High
Schools, and Elementary Schools within the District as may be determined by
mutual agreement between the Department and the District.   Officers assigned to
these locations shall perform routine police services during regular school hours.
Officers will also conduct a drug/alcohol awareness program as may be
determined by mutual agreement between the Department and the District.
```

### Page 3 of 3

```text
b.
Officers at athletic events, school dances, and other special events as may be
determined by mutual agreement between the Department and the District,
subject to the availability of Department personnel.

c.
If any school officer is absent for ten (10) or more consecutive school days, the
Department will provide a replacement officer to cover the officer’s duty
assignment.

d.
Except as provided by Paragraph 9 of this Agreement, police officers assigned to
provide services under this Agreement shall devote substantially all of their
working time to the District during regular school hours and at such other times
as may be determined by mutual agreement between the Department and the
District.

12.
This Agreement shall not be modified or altered unless mutually agreed upon by the
parties in writing.

13.
This Agreement contains the entire understanding of the parties.  There are no
understandings between the parties, written or otherwise, not contained herein.  Each party acknowledges
that they have consulted with, or have had the opportunity to consult with, legal counsel regarding this
Agreement.

14.
If any provision, section, subsection, sentence, clause or phrase of this Agreement is
invalidated by any court of competent jurisdiction, such a holding shall not affect the validity of the
remainder of the Agreement, which shall continue in full force and effect.

IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties hereto have caused this instrument to be executed as of the
day and year first above written.

CITY OF CHEYENNE
BY:

